# PROJECT MASTER RECORD — MANDATORY PHASE UPDATE

The file:

V2/project_record/PROJECT_MASTER_RECORD.md

is the authoritative chronological record of the V2 project.

AFTER EVERY COMPLETED PHASE:

1. Verify the phase is actually complete.
2. Review the implementation, tests, configuration and outputs produced by that phase.
3. Update PROJECT_MASTER_RECORD.md before declaring the phase complete.
4. Add a new chronological section:

## Phase X — [Phase Name]

Include:
- Date
- Objective
- Why the phase was required
- Work completed
- Technical decisions
- Files created/modified
- Tests/validation
- Actual outcome
- Problems encountered
- Problems resolved
- Remaining issues
- Dissertation relevance
- Evidence/source file paths

5. Update the relevant sections of the master record with newly verified information.
6. Mark unknown or unverified information as:
   NEEDS VERIFICATION

7. Never invent results or settings.
8. Never overwrite historical phase summaries.
9. If a later phase changes a previous assumption, preserve the historical entry and add the correction/change to the Decisions Log.
10. Do not declare a phase complete until the master record has been updated.

11. Record **backup status** for the completed phase:
    - Colab / Google Drive / Local / GitHub (verified paths only)
    - local backup recommendation
    - GitHub commit recommendation
    Use format in `V2/project_record/PHASE_COMPLETION_BACKUP_TEMPLATE.md`.
    Never claim a backup exists unless verified.

12. Stop before beginning the next phase.

The master record must always reflect the actual implemented project, not merely the original plan.

Actual code, configuration, experiment outputs and test results take precedence over previous AI summaries or assumptions.
